WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:05.210
Barack Obama gave a number of interviews,
including to CBS's 60 Minutes, which we will

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:09.310
get to, but also to Gayle King.

00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:14.349
And it was very interesting to hear Barack
Obama's perspective on the last four years

00:00:14.349 --> 00:00:20.340
and on the election that Joe Biden has defeated
Donald Trump and the implications.

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:24.821
And one of the messages that Barack Obama
focused on, not just in this interview, but

00:00:24.821 --> 00:00:29.510
in others as well, is that this is not normal
and it's an important message.

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:32.910
We've been talking about hyper normalization
for four years.

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.070
Let's take a listen to the former president
here.

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:43.570
I think we were in a circumstance in this
election in which certain norms, certain institutional

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:52.260
values that are so extraordinarily important
had been breached that it was important for

00:00:52.260 --> 00:01:00.250
me as somebody who had served in that office
to simply let people know this is not normal.

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:03.680
So I've talked about this and I talked about
this when Donald Trump was elected and we

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.820
saw things are going to be insane.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:10.830
I started saying I am going to try to prevent
the normalization of insanity.

00:01:10.830 --> 00:01:15.020
And it's something we've continued talking
about and we've had to fight and it happens

00:01:15.020 --> 00:01:16.590
to all of us.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:25.030
There is no way to see daily scandal and embarrassment
and humiliation day after day after day and

00:01:25.030 --> 00:01:30.990
not to some degree become desensitized to
it, to another attack on the media, to another

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:36.030
attack on democracy, to another attack on
the sort of fundamentals that this country

00:01:36.030 --> 00:01:37.030
is based on.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:40.860
And Barack Obama nicely lays out, this is
not normal.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:42.250
None of this is normal.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:49.759
And Barack Obama also lays out that he's very
concerned about the 72 million people that

00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:56.659
voted for Donald Trump, whose world view is
largely informed by radical right wing media,

00:01:56.659 --> 00:02:00.630
exactly as I've been talking about for the
last several months.

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:02.080
Take a listen to this.

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:04.900
Seventy two million people voted for Donald
Trump.

00:02:04.900 --> 00:02:07.409
What does that say to you about the state
of this country?

00:02:07.409 --> 00:02:10.420
Well, what it says is that we are still deeply
divided.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:20.590
The power of that alternative worldview that's
presented in the media that those voters consume,

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:22.150
it carries a lot of weight.

00:02:22.150 --> 00:02:23.440
Are you worried about that?

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:24.440
Yes.

00:02:24.440 --> 00:02:32.370
It's very hard for our democracy to function
if we are operating on just completely different

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:33.560
sets of facts.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:37.660
But it's clear as we sit here today, we're
not going to have a peaceful transition.

00:02:37.660 --> 00:02:42.560
I think about John McCain calling George and
Laura Bush welcoming you and Michelle Obama

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.349
to the White House could not have been more
gracious.

00:02:44.349 --> 00:02:47.170
I remember you inviting Donald Trump to the
White House.

00:02:47.170 --> 00:02:49.840
If you succeed, then the country succeeds.

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:53.730
I wish that you succeed because we want the
country to succeed.

00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:57.350
He does not seem to have taken a page out
of any of those playbooks.

00:02:57.350 --> 00:02:58.350
No.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:00.400
So what is at stake here?

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:03.810
Well, look, Joe Biden will be the next president
of United States.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:05.600
Kamala Harris will be the next vice president.

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:07.170
There is no legal basis.

00:03:07.170 --> 00:03:10.840
There's no getting support from members of
the Republican Party who are not challenging

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:11.840
him.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:14.760
And that has been disappointing.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.940
But it's been sort of par for the course during
these four years.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:21.530
They obviously didn't think there was any
fraud going on because they didn't say anything

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:22.840
about it for the first two days.

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:26.909
Barack Obama was also asked about his demeanor
on the campaign trail when he was out there

00:03:26.909 --> 00:03:29.300
for Joe Biden over the last few weeks.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:33.659
And Barack Obama pointed out that he was not
so much going in on Trump.

00:03:33.659 --> 00:03:34.730
He was stating facts.

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:37.190
He was just repeating things, Trump said verbatim.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:38.580
It wasn't personal, actually.

00:03:38.580 --> 00:03:40.940
What you didn't have I've had it moment.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:43.670
The truth is everything I said, I was just
stating facts.

00:03:43.670 --> 00:03:45.200
You've got a president right now.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:48.280
He wants full credit for an economy that he
inherited.

00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:51.550
He wants zero blame for the pandemic he ignored.

00:03:51.550 --> 00:03:54.450
It was out of character for you to speak up,
Mr. President.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:04:02.140
That way I was not the person who, at a White
House briefing room said, how is Bletch the

00:04:02.140 --> 00:04:03.239
way to solve it?

00:04:03.239 --> 00:04:04.750
I wasn't doing a routine.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:07.730
I was repeating words that I heard.

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:14.280
We talked about how it is really difficult
to massively deprogram millions of.

00:04:14.280 --> 00:04:19.430
Lists and case in point, last week I took
a very interesting call from from a fellow

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:24.669
YouTube who has a small channel who said,
David, I was able to do it.

00:04:24.669 --> 00:04:29.930
I'd programed a trumpet and I said, great,
well, so how did it happen?

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:37.599
And the guy said, well, I had him on my YouTube
channel for three hours for a one on one conversation.

00:04:37.599 --> 00:04:43.319
And that is a very difficult timeline for
the massive deprogramming of 72 million people.

00:04:43.319 --> 00:04:46.729
Now, you can say you don't have to deprogram
all 72 million.

00:04:46.729 --> 00:04:52.069
If you can deprogram 10, 15 percent of them,
you're already shifting the electoral balance

00:04:52.069 --> 00:04:53.069
dramatically.

00:04:53.069 --> 00:04:58.249
But the first step to massive deprogramming
has to be massive normalization.

00:04:58.249 --> 00:05:06.080
It has to be the masses must re realize they
must again come to realize that this is not

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:07.830
normal, that it's whacked.

00:05:07.830 --> 00:05:09.800
I don't really know how to do it.

00:05:09.800 --> 00:05:15.169
One thing I thought about over the weekend
was with the realization that Trump doesn't

00:05:15.169 --> 00:05:18.029
care about them, play a role in the deprogramming.

00:05:18.029 --> 00:05:24.639
And what I mean by that is Donald Trump's
supporters are people that Trump wouldn't

00:05:24.639 --> 00:05:26.300
be caught dead with.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:32.580
Most of Trump supporters are people Trump
has spent his entire life avoiding by flying

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:38.680
private and living where he has lived and
so on and so forth.

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.840
And you just have to look at this weekend
for a perfect example.

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:46.860
There was this big protest in favor of Trump
in D.C., people going crazy.

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.889
And we'll talk about that a little bit later.

00:05:48.889 --> 00:05:54.229
Trump literally drives by the protest, waving
from inside his armored vehicle on his way

00:05:54.229 --> 00:05:56.229
to spend the weekend playing golf.

00:05:56.229 --> 00:05:57.520
He doesn't care about them.

00:05:57.520 --> 00:05:59.689
And I'm just thinking out loud here.

00:05:59.689 --> 00:06:05.249
If Trump supporters came to really understand
that Trump doesn't give to, you know, what's

00:06:05.249 --> 00:06:07.991
about them, would that help to deprogram them?

00:06:07.991 --> 00:06:12.740
And I'm reminded of an LBJ quote, Lyndon B.
Johnson, the former president, who said, if

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:17.069
you can convince the lowest white man that
he's better than the best colored man, this

00:06:17.069 --> 00:06:19.399
was the vocabulary of the time.

00:06:19.399 --> 00:06:21.440
He won't notice you're picking his pocket.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:27.589
Hell, give him somebody to look down on and
he'll empty his pockets for you.

00:06:27.589 --> 00:06:31.710
That's who Trump has targeted and who primarily
has to be deprogrammed.

00:06:31.710 --> 00:06:36.210
So, bottom line, I'm glad Barack Obama is
saying these things.

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:41.969
I'm disgusted and horrified that things like
this have to be said, that it has to be mentioned.

00:06:41.969 --> 00:06:47.619
Trump continuing to claim he won is a disaster
for the for the United States.

00:06:47.619 --> 00:06:49.279
It's an embarrassment.

00:06:49.279 --> 00:06:53.419
Trump attacking the media, Trump attacking
these fundamental institutions.

00:06:53.419 --> 00:06:56.259
The fact that we have to mention, hey, guys,
by the way, this is bad.

00:06:56.259 --> 00:06:57.709
This isn't normal.

00:06:57.709 --> 00:06:59.089
That's the tragedy.

00:06:59.089 --> 00:07:02.179
And a peaceful transfer of power, of course,
is important.

00:07:02.179 --> 00:07:06.430
Joe Biden, one that's not a controversial
thing to say, or at least it shouldn't be.

00:07:06.430 --> 00:07:11.849
But 86 percent of Trump voters don't believe
that Joe Biden legitimately won.

00:07:11.849 --> 00:08:35.430
I imagine that as we get closer to inauguration,
that number will decline.

